## Context

These modules are partially covered, but the untested lines are the
risky branches (retry/backoff, malformed responses, error paths):

- `build_corpus.py` (27%) — Zotero HTTP fetch (`_zotero_get`,
  `zotero_search`, `zotero_download_pdf`), `score_section`, and the whole
  `main()` (`:342-559`). Needs `httpx` mocking; section/selection logic
  is already covered.
- `worker.py` (78%) — `_execute_decomposed` (`:669-699`) and `main()`
  (`:883-936`) untested; other `_execute_*` arms are covered.
  Decomposed-arm execution is a real behavioral gap.
- `query_anthropic.py` (65%) — `dispatch`/`_call_with_retry`
  (`:400-453`, `:533-596`) and malformed-response parsing.
- `adapter_openai_responses.py` (59%) — response-parsing edge cases
  (`:433-560`).

Retry/backoff and malformed-response handling are exactly where adapters
break in production.

## Approach

- Mock `httpx`/client objects; assert retry count, backoff schedule,
  and graceful handling of 5xx / truncated JSON.
- For `worker._execute_decomposed`, drive it with a fake client and a
  decomposed `JobSpec`, assert the result/record shape.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `_call_with_retry` retry-exhaustion + backoff path tested.
- [ ] `worker._execute_decomposed` has a happy-path test.
- [ ] Adapter response parsers tested against a malformed/truncated payload.
- [ ] `make test-fast` passes.

## Out of scope

- Live network calls (keep these in `slow`-marked tests if added at all).
